  "question": {
    "text": "In an ammeter, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the main current passes through the galvanometer. If resistance of the galvanometer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the resistance of ammeter will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mn>20</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mn>199</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>199</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0043_9b2692d82f61.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 130px;\"/></p><p>As potential drop across both branches would be the same, we get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>95</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>I</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>I</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>G</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>G</mi><mn>19</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, resistance of ammeter will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfrac><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>19</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mi>G</mi></mrow><mn>19</mn></mfrac></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>G</mi><mn>20</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}